  "narrative": "I continue to interpret signed estimates as follows: for direction -1 claims, a positive estimate means stronger measured dependency in the exposed group, i.e. a more negative raw dependency_composite; for direction +1 claims, a positive estimate means a higher/less-negative raw composite, i.e. weaker measured dependency. The new results strongly support context independence among the largest central marker associations. H76 shows that within SMARCA4-loss cells, TP53 loss remains associated with weaker measured dependency (+0.897, CI +0.789 to +1.005). H77 shows that within SMARCA4-loss cells, KEAP1 loss also remains associated with weaker measured dependency (+0.790, CI +0.661 to +0.920). These are far above the 0.15-unit threshold, so the broad TP53 and KEAP1 weaker-dependency associations are not merely artifacts of their absence inside SMARCA4-loss cells. I accept and close both as context-robustness tests.\n\nThe reciprocal SMARCA4/MSI-high checks are also decisive. H53 shows SMARCA4 loss remains strongly associated with stronger measured dependency within MSI-high cells (+0.785, CI +0.580 to +0.990), and H78 shows MSI-high remains strongly associated with stronger measured dependency within SMARCA4-loss cells (+0.748, CI +0.562 to +0.935). Despite the small exposed MSI-high cell counts, both intervals remain far above threshold. Similarly, H79 shows MSI-high within TP53-loss cells remains a large stronger-dependency association (+0.749, CI +0.526 to +0.971), and H80 shows MSI-high within KEAP1-loss cells remains a large stronger-dependency association (+0.925, CI +0.698 to +1.151). These tests are imprecise relative to broader tests but are still far above threshold, and they are highly consistent with earlier MSI-high results. I accept and close them as robustness/context-independence evidence rather than as separate novel mechanisms.\n\nThe histologic PTEN tests are more cautious. H81 tests PTEN loss in adenocarcinoma cells and gives +0.227 (CI +0.121 to +0.333), while H82 tests PTEN loss in squamous cells and gives +0.268 (CI +0.075 to +0.461). Both point estimates are in the expected stronger-dependency direction and are above the 0.15-unit threshold, but both intervals include values below threshold. The broad PTEN main effect remains accepted and independently validated, so these results are supportive rather than decisive. I keep the histologic subgroup claims unresolved and deferred because they should not be treated as confirmed threshold-level context effects on the basis of these intervals alone.\n\nThe CDKN2A results do not establish a robust scientifically meaningful predictor. H72 broad CDKN2A loss is below the threshold: +0.139 (CI +0.065 to +0.213). H73 within TP53-intact cells is also below threshold: +0.125 (CI +0.051 to +0.199). H74 within TP53-loss cells is above threshold in point estimate, +0.188, but highly imprecise and crosses the threshold boundary (CI +0.045 to +0.332). H75 in non-Avana library cells is small and imprecise, +0.068 (CI -0.140 to +0.275). Taken together with earlier clean-stratum CDKN2A estimates, the pattern is borderline, context-sensitive, and not sufficiently precise to accept. I leave these unresolved but deferred rather than accepting CDKN2A as a residual predictor.\n\nGiven the strength and breadth of the TP53-loss evidence, including the new context-robust test H76, I request independent validation of H11, the overall TP53-loss main effect. This is the highest-value unvalidated central association. If validation confirms, the main TP53 weaker-dependency association can be closed; the next main validation target should then be H10 MSI-high. Multiplicity remains relevant, but the accepted new effects are far above the effect-size threshold and directionally consistent with earlier evidence, whereas near-threshold CDKN2A and histologic PTEN subgroup claims remain unresolved. All conclusions remain dataset-level associations, not causal effects or claims of external generalizability.",
  "research_notes": "Appraise update. Signed convention: direction -1 positive = stronger measured dependency; direction +1 positive = higher/less-negative composite = weaker measured dependency.\n\nCentral accepted dataset-level associations: SMARCA4 loss -> strong stronger dependency, main accepted and validated; KEAP1 loss -> strong weaker dependency, main accepted and validated; TP53 loss -> strong weaker dependency, very robust across contexts but main H11 not yet independently validated; MSI_high -> strong stronger dependency, robust across contexts but main H10 not yet independently validated; PTEN loss -> moderate stronger dependency, main accepted and validated.\n\nNew context-independence results support approximate independence among central marker axes rather than proxy artifacts: TP53 loss within SMARCA4-loss H76 (+0.897, CI +0.789 to +1.005) accepted/closed; KEAP1 loss within SMARCA4-loss H77 (+0.790, CI +0.661 to +0.920) accepted/closed. SMARCA4/MSI reciprocal tests accepted/closed: H53 SMARCA4 within MSI_high (+0.785, CI +0.580 to +0.990); H78 MSI_high within SMARCA4-loss (+0.748, CI +0.562 to +0.935). MSI_high within TP53-loss H79 (+0.749, CI +0.526 to +0.971) and within KEAP1-loss H80 (+0.925, CI +0.698 to +1.151) accepted/closed despite small exposed cells because intervals are far above threshold.\n\nPTEN histology: H81 adenocarcinoma +0.227 CI +0.121 to +0.333; H82 squamous +0.268 CI +0.075 to +0.461. Point estimates supportive of accepted PTEN main effect, but intervals cross the 0.15-unit threshold, so subgroup claims remain unresolved/deferred. Do not interpret these as confirmed threshold-level histologic context effects.\n\nCDKN2A: overall pattern is borderline and not accepted. Broad H72 +0.139 CI +0.065 to +0.213; TP53-intact H73 +0.125 CI +0.051 to +0.199; TP53-loss H74 +0.188 CI +0.045 to +0.332; non-Avana H75 +0.068 CI -0.140 to +0.275. Clean-stratum H42 +0.168 CI +0.100 to +0.235 and cleaner H54 +0.148 CI +0.093 to +0.204 are similarly borderline. CDKN2A remains unresolved/deferred, not a central accepted predictor, because point estimates straddle the threshold and several intervals include values below threshold.\n\nValidation request: H11 TP53 loss main effect. It is the highest-value remaining unvalidated central association and is now supported by many robustness contexts, including H76. Next validation priority: H10 MSI_high. If H11 validates, accept and close main TP53. Residual clean tests H58 APC, H59 NF1, H71 SMAD4 are lower priority unless a future analysis reveals a large precise signal. All conclusions remain dataset-level associations, not causal mechanisms or external generalizability.",
